<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <application
        android:allowBackup="true"
        android:label="Valo Deep Links"
        android:theme="@android:style/Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true"
            android:launchMode="singleTop">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>

            <!--
                DEEP LINKS: "open MainActivity for any link that starts with valo://app"

                An intent-filter tells Android which Intents this Activity accepts.
                A link is sent as an Intent, so ALL 4 lines below must match:

                  action VIEW         = "show this link". Browsers, apps and adb all use it.

                  category DEFAULT    = REQUIRED. Android adds it to every startActivity()
                                        call. Forget it and the link never opens the app.

                  category BROWSABLE  = lets a browser (like Chrome) open the app.
                                        Without it, adb works but tapping a link doesn't.

                  data scheme + host  = which links: valo://app/... (any path after it).

                There's no path here on purpose. The manifest only says "this app handles
                valo://app". The NavController picks the SCREEN from the rest of the link
                (/agent/..., /career), using navDeepLink in ValoNavApp.kt.
                So adding a new linkable screen needs no change here.

                valo:// is a custom link type: easy to test, no website needed.
                Real apps often use normal https:// links ("App Links") instead. Those need
                android:autoVerify="true" and a file on your website to prove you own it.

                On the <activity> above:
                  exported="true"         = other apps may open this Activity. Needed for the
                                            home screen icon AND for links. It also means
                                            anyone can send any link, so check the values.
                  launchMode="singleTop"  = if the app is already open, reuse it instead of
                                            starting a second copy. The new link then arrives
                                            in onNewIntent(), and ValoNavApp handles it.
            -->
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.BROWSABLE" />
                <data android:scheme="valo" android:host="app" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>

</manifest>
